From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:32:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: Add Apple A9 display pipe
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Apple A9 SoCs (S8000/S8003) drive their internal eDP panel from the
disp0 display subsystem, an ADP/ADBE pipe without a display coprocessor.
The bootloader leaves the pipe, the eDP link and the panel running.

Describe the six register windows and five interrupts from the Apple
device tree ("adbe0,s8000"), and the two power domains the pipe and its
eDP output need. Powering either off resets the pipe and the link.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 71a3dfd5 (J71t ledger 11.1); compatible
 renamed to apple,s8000-display-pipe after the apple,h7-display-pipe
 pattern, power-domains described instead of kept out of the node, the
 boot VRAM memory-region dropped (the driver finds the boot framebuffer
 through the simple-framebuffer node).]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
